\label{prop-merom-q-existence-1}	
	Let $U \subset C$ be an open subset, $i\in \{1, 2\}$, $d = 3g-4 + i$, and
	$\mathbf{x}^d: U \rightarrow C^{[d]}$, $x \mapsto \mathbf{x}^d(x) = x_1(x) + ... + x_d(x)$,
	be a holomorphic map such that, 
	for all $x\in U$ and $r \in \{1 , ..., d\}$,
	$x_r(x) \neq x$ 
	and $\mathbf{x}^d(x)$ is $Q$-generic.
	Then there exists a family of meromorphic quadratic differentials $\left\{ q^{(i)}_{x, \mathbf{x}^d} \right\}_{x \in U}$ 
	holomorphically parameterized by $U$ such that 
		\begin{enumerate}[(a)]
			\item $q^{(i)}_{x, \mathbf{x}^d}$ has a simple (double) pole at $x$ if $i=1$ (respectively, $i=2$) and is holomorphic on $C\setminus \{x\}$;
			\item $\mathbf{x}^d(x)$ is contained in the support of the zero divisor of $q^{(i)}_{x, \mathbf{x}^d}$.
		\end{enumerate}

